1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
A chain of mud towers once outran every horse.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:04,000
I'm your China Travel Expert.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Along the Han Wall, a tower rose every 5 km.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Smoke by day, fire by night — a signal chain.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
A rider covered about 300 li a day.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The fire leapt tower to tower — far faster.

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,600
Double-tap if you'd walk this desert wall.

8
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,000
★ Expert Tip: See them near Dunhuang — over 80 towers still stand.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Next: a temple carved straight into a cliff.
